// Single-action schema: the only action is Transfer, so the temporal
// predicate necessarily self-references the decision action. Permit a
// Transfer only when the immediately preceding timepoint was also a
// Transfer by the SAME user (`previous`, not `formerly`, because with one
// action a `formerly` self-match is vacuously true at every timepoint —
// the current event always matches).
//
// Trace: Transfer(alice @0) -> Transfer(alice @10) -> Transfer(bob @20)
//        -> Transfer(bob @30).
// tp0: no previous timepoint            -> false
// tp1: previous is alice's, user=alice  -> true
// tp2: previous is alice's, user=bob    -> false (pin mismatch)
// tp3: previous is bob's, user=bob      -> true

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 1h Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
